<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch state raises price of Feb 2007 bond to 99.70.</title>
<headline>Dutch state raises price of Feb 2007 bond to 99.70.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch Finance Ministry's capital markets agency raised the price of the 5.75 percent bond due February 2007 to 99.70 on the second day of tap sales on Wednesday, from 99.55 at the close on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The capital markets agency said on Tuesday that 1.9 billion guilders had been raised so far through tap sales.</p>
<p>Tap sales of the bond, first issued in January, reopened on Tuesday and will continue daily between 0700 GMT and 1500 GMT until further notice.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
